 {'clause':'Exact far-triple occurrence and uniqueness','assessment':'By definition a farTriple reads the current coordinate interval endpoints and its actual interior cut. Equality to the critical triple therefore implies that the coordinate interval equals [x,z] and the actual interiorPosition equals y; conversely these equalities imply equality of all three triple entries. The interior-position map is injective by strict cut ordering, hence the far-triple map is injective. Existence of the critical far triple is equivalent to whole-span equality and actual middle-cut membership: the strict x<y<z bounds ensure middle membership is interior membership, and the existing exact interior-index equivalence supplies its unique index. The independent middle-composition consumer also derives parts>=2, so the existential index is nonvacuous and the unary composition cannot accidentally contain an interior critical gate.'},
